bug in `ledger/currency.py`. `to_cents` used `int(amount * 100)`, which truncates. Floats such as `19.99` and `0.29` come out slightly below the true value (for example 1998.999\u2026), so results were a cent or more short. It now converts through `Decimal(str(amount))` and rounds half up.\n\nThe full suite passes (5 tests, including `tests/test_report.py`). The three failing tests were all caused by this one function, so I didn't touch the tax or discount code.\n\nOne assumption: prices arrive as `float` or `Decimal`, and their `str()` form is the decimal value you intend. For example, `str(19.99)` is `\"19.99\"`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 107597, "requests_cache_write": 17228, "requests_cost_usd": 0.0686477, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1479, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial14", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 87, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-17T23:18:37.887704+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 16.044, "t_checker_s": 0.324, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1493, "tokens_cache_read": 107597, "tokens_cache_write": 17228, "tokens_fresh": 1493, "tokens_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_cache_read": 107597, "tokens_main_cache_write": 17228, "tokens_main_calls": 6, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 14, "tokens_main_output": 1479, "tokens_output": 1479, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 107597, "tokens_proxy_cache_wr